          "link rel=canonical tells a search engine the primary URL when you have sort parameters, http versus https, a trailing slash, or a print version. The canonical URL must be absolute and must point at a page that actually returns 200, not a redirect loop. rel=hreflang lists language variants of the same page (uk, en, x-default) and each variant must point at all the others, including itself. A broken hreflang (a non-existent language, a one-way link) is ignored. canonical is not a substitute for a 301 if you have permanently moved.",
          ["canonical — абсолютний головний URL із відповіддю 200", "hreflang взаємний між усіма мовними версіями", "Для переїзду адреси — 301, не лише canonical"],
